{
 "plan_sha256_8": "e6326d34",
 "base": "origin/main 43447659a3 + claude/path-kv-sysc2-1025@becb8f371d (sysc2 does not touch die_plan.json)",
 "die_grt_evidence": "DIE-FT it5 epyc1:/srv/opentallas-scratch2/claude/die-ft-1830/qwen_kvsys (ovf 816,190 M6 418,373 / M7 397,815; 2D hot gcells 152)",
 "finding_1_window_density": "v3.9 (ee1aee20, die GRT 0) packed every N/S/E/W ft window at 5.1-5.2 bits/um; v3.9g/f7ch channel-mouth packing (face_pins_per_um 13.2, G2-proven at partition level) packs them at 11.4-12.5 bits/um. Die-GRT share capacity (adj 0.75 on M4-M7) is 0.25*(1/0.048+1/0.064)=9.11 bits/um per direction, so every window >9.1/um overflows in the die model. W-column hgi N/S faces carry 12,846+7,494 bits in such windows; the E column carries none (E hgi types have no >9.1/um N/S window) -> the asymmetry of the ovf map.",
 "finding_2_channel_budget": "hgi W column (hgi_v6/v7/v8) has 4 full-height core-free x channels (233-337, 553-657, 873-976 um, plus the 86-um E strip 1192-1279 and the 17-um W strip). N-S ft through every row boundary = 3,461 bits = 0.92 of the die-share channel capacity (3,776); channels c2 (ft4 L663 1044 b) 1.10 and c3 (ft9 L751 549 + ft23 L2048 523) 1.13 are over 1.0 even if spread over the full mouth; at the hgi_WN_7|hub_Wi boundary c1-c3 are 1.11-1.14 (hgi_v8 also jogs L663/L350 from c1 to c2 = the chan3 G2 FAIL). hg W column (hg/hg_v1/hg_v3) carries 2,451 bits at 0.60-0.70. Both W columns together: 5,912 bits / 7,552 = 0.78.",
 "conclusion": "Respreading windows inside the current mouths cannot reach overflow 0: c2/c3 stay >1.0 of the die share. The structural fix needs capacity-constrained channel assignment across BOTH W columns (hg + hgi) -- e.g. move L2048 (523 b serdes_W rx, source sys_SW/io_W2 side) and ~half of L751 or L1524 into the hg column channels (io_W2 -> hg_WN_0..7 -> hub_Wo -> hub_Wi), which is a lane re-path (ft slots added to kv3_hg/hg_v1/hg_v3, removed from hgi_v6/v7/v8; hub_Wo|hub_Wi and io_W2|io_W3 crossings), target every channel <= ~0.8 and every window <= 9.1/um (<= 7.5/um preferred). Alternative (b): widen the hgi channels (head-core column pitch) -- outline growth. Alternative (c): COORD/DIE-FT model ruling (see model_note).",
 "model_note": "die_trial.core_obs obstructs a planned core only to M5 unless it has a LEF, but kv3_head_eighth_* harden with sigmax M7 (cores/harden/recipes_kv.json) and g2.probe_blockages already obstructs them to M7. So the die GRT is optimistic over head cores (M6/M7 free) and pessimistic inside channels (25% share, M1-M3 removed) -- the v3.9 zero was obtained by spilling over the head cores, which the real cores do not allow.",
